{
  "_comment": "Golden vectors for normalize_repository (framework_sessions.py). The CLI parses the git remote itself and sends the parsed id as repo_remote, so a value that is not a URL or an scp form passes through, stripped and lower-cased, with all its segments. URL and scp forms are still parsed with the CLI rules, for older or other writers: expected is what detectGitRemoteRepo (src/utils/processes.ts, function parseGitRemoteUrl) of codemie-code returns for the raw git remote; when it returns undefined, or the remote is empty, normalize_repository falls back to the working directory, and with an empty working directory gives 'unknown' (the bucket the CLI reports). Regenerate it whenever the CLI rule changes. source cli_test: input and expected come from the CLI test src/utils/__tests__/processes-git.test.ts; source cli_run: expected was produced by running the CLI function with node (for a parsed id: truncateProjectPath of the built CLI returns it unchanged apart from the lower-casing the Python side applies); source contract: the Python-side rule, not a CLI output (a pass-through of a bare path or other non-URL value, and 'unknown' where the CLI function returns undefined).",
